cff-version: 1.2.0
title: >-
  MarketLab: a prospective, reproducible platform for studying memory and
  reflection in decision-making LLM agents
message: >-
  If you use this software or its design in your research, please cite it. If
  you cite results produced with it, please also state which model was used and
  which pre-registration applied — see docs/PRE_REGISTRATION.md.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Gallusser
    given-names: Noah
    alias: zolaski333
license: MIT
version: 0.1.0
date-released: "2026-08-08"
repository-code: "https://github.com/zolaski333/marketlab"
abstract: >-
  MarketLab studies whether persistent memory and periodic strategic reflection
  improve the probabilistic quality, coherence and stability of an LLM agent's
  decisions in a virtual multi-asset market. It is prospective and
  point-in-time correct by construction: nothing an agent reads was visible
  later than the instant it decided. The design is a crossed 2x2 of (memory,
  reflection) with matched placebos, run against a shared frozen snapshot so
  that a difference between conditions cannot be a difference in what they were
  shown. Financial performance is a secondary, exploratory measure; a positive
  return is never treated as evidence of competence. No real money is ever
  involved and no investment advice is produced.
keywords:
  - large language models
  - agents
  - forecasting
  - calibration
  - reproducibility
  - pre-registration
  - virtual market
